  /*
   * Single source of truth for vertical dropdown/panel positioning.
   *
   * Every dropdown in the plugin must open downward when there is room below
   * the anchor and flip upward when near the bottom of the viewport. This used
   * to be reimplemented ~23 times inline, each with its own fallback height and
   * — critically — some measuring the panel height BEFORE it was appended to the
   * DOM (where outerHeight() returns 0 and a wrong fallback was used), which is
   * why some dropdowns floated detached or clipped.
   *
   * wcbatFlipTop() takes the panel (which MUST already be in the DOM) and the
   * anchor's bounding rect, measures the real height, and returns the correct
   * fixed `top`. Callers own their own horizontal (left/width) logic; this owns
   * the vertical flip so it is identical everywhere.
   *
   * Usage:
   *   $panel.appendTo("body");                 // append FIRST
   *   var top = wcbatFlipTop($panel, rect);    // then measure + flip
   *   $panel.css({ position:"fixed", top:top+"px", left:... });
   */
